From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:28:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Herring-Vogt valleys follow the crystal orientation

build_charge_tensors built the valley rotation matrices from the crystal-frame
valley_dirs, while all charge vectors (p, E, v) are in the detector frame, so
with a non-identity CrystalConfig::orient (e.g. set_miller_orientation) the
valleys were misplaced (velocity error up to 15x |v| in tests/test_charge_misc).
Valley axes are now rotated by orient, as G4LatticePhysical does for the
lattice-to-local transform (Herring & Vogt 1956 / Leman 1109.1193 Eq. (23)
[FT] define T in the valley frame). Test: tests/test_charge_misc.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BcNoovRae5kkbL36KL3sYy
---
 include/cmpmc/lattice.hpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/cmpmc/lattice.hpp b/include/cmpmc/lattice.hpp
index 69a3de6..7d47d9a 100644
--- a/include/cmpmc/lattice.hpp
+++ b/include/cmpmc/lattice.hpp
@@ -404,7 +404,9 @@ private:
 
         valley_rot_.clear();
         for (const Vec3& raw_dir : cfg_.valley_dirs) {
-            const Vec3 vdir = raw_dir.unit();
+            // valley_dirs are crystal-frame axes; all charge vectors (p, E, v) live in
+            // the detector frame, so rotate the axis with the crystal orientation.
+            const Vec3 vdir = (cfg_.orient * raw_dir.unit()).unit();
             const double vx = vdir.x;
             const double vy = vdir.y;
             const double vz = vdir.z;
